WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
The technology and semantics underneath: tailoring forms beyond hand programming meets knowledge representation

2
00:02:04.000 --> 00:04:53.000
SMK, later GRAIL - a language for 'conceptual Lego'; frame systems and tangled semantic networks

3
00:04:53.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Inheriting the most specific things and collecting them onto a form (the hypertension example)

4
00:07:07.000 --> 00:09:20.000
Extrinsics in GALEN, and normalizing the ontology: primitive trees stuck together with properties

5
00:09:20.000 --> 00:13:17.000
Pulling apart part-whole, function and structure - primitive hierarchies without exceptions (supernumerary fingers, dextrocardia: 'it's biology, not physics')

6
00:13:17.000 --> 00:16:11.000
Classifiers and most specific generalizations (more in the 'On beyond Gruber' paper)

7
00:16:11.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Collecting forms, treatments and codes (ICD, Read codes); negation in description logics and the need for queries

8
00:18:42.000 --> 00:21:32.000
Querying an OWL ontology - the 'hypertension not in pregnancy' trap

9
00:21:32.000 --> 00:24:58.000
Why check after classification? Errors propagate - getting the foot out of the pelvis in SNOMED

10
00:24:58.000 --> 00:28:49.000
12 hours per classifier run - regression queries 'just like software testing'; user interfaces and language generation as QA

11
00:28:49.000 --> 00:34:02.000
Pre- or post-coordination? Clean, normalized hierarchies; axioms vs generalizations (penicillins, Tweety the bird)

12
00:34:02.000 --> 00:35:51.000
Modular ontologies and property patterns - contributions to OWL

13
00:35:51.000 --> 00:40:10.000
Final words for techies: the same technique in ICD-11, queries to coordinate SNOMED and ICD, 'rigid' properties

14
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:16.240
The end
